From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:26:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Derive a mentioned-only GT raster namespace
 (language-reachable ceiling)

A GT r1.5 m map paints everything along the route; a map predicted from
the instruction can at best contain the categories the instruction names.
make_mentioned_only_gt_cache.py zeroes, per episode, the channels of
categories the project's instruction extractor (prior.grid_map._cognitive
.extract_categories, the one behind the GT 'mentioned' flags) does not
find in the instruction, keeping layout and metadata, and writes
<namespace>.mentioned_only. Evaluating the GT-trained try5 policy on it
(training-free) gives the ceiling a perfect language-predicted map could
reach under that policy; the gap to the full GT map is content no
instruction carries.

